  "appeal_decision": null,
  "description": "Installation of two small compact, low-noise, high-efficiency outdoor air conditioning condenser units on the private side balcony of a top-floor flat.\n\nThe units will be discreetly positioned more than 1.4 metres from the flat balcony edge, on the railway-facing side of the property, fully within the demise of the flat. The nearest habitable window of any neighbouring property is over 20 metres away, and the units are not visible from the public road due to the height and layout of the building. They are also not visible from the side, due to the elevation and architectural design.\n\nExternal Unit Dimensions:\n- M2OE-18HFN8-Q: 80.5 cm (W) × 33.0 cm (D) × 55.4 cm (H)\n- AG2Eco-12N8D0-O: 72.0 cm (W) × 27.0 cm (D) × 49.5 cm (H)\n\nBoth models have a maximum sound pressure level of ≤55 dB(A) at 1 meter, per manufacturer specifications. Accounting for distance attenuation calculations, the predicted noise level as per the manufacturer at the nearest sensitive receptor (20+ metres away) is approximately 25–30 dB(A), which is at least 10 dB below the typical residential background level of 35–40 dB(A), in compliance with BS4142:2014. The units will also be mounted on certified anti-vibration feet to further reduce disturbance.\n\nThere will be no visual impact on the building or streetscape. The units are compact, neutral in colour, and located on a recessed side balcony—not mounted on any public-facing wall, shared wall, or roofline. Photos and annotated elevation drawings demonstrate their concealed placement and minimal visibility.\n\nInstallation will be carried out by a qualified and insured contractor (Jensen Property Maintenance Ltd) and will comply with all relevant building regulations, including electrical safety, waterproofing, and fire protection. Building control sign-off will be obtained as required by the freeholder.\n\nThe proposal will not result in any loss of light or privacy to neighbouring residents. The equipment is well separated from all windows and situated over 1.4 meters from the roof edge.\n\nThe selected systems are low-carbon and ultra energy efficient, SEER A++ rated, and use high-efficiency heat pump technology for both cooling and heating. Fully green electric operation supports reduced winter energy use and lower emissions compared to gas-based systems.\n\nThe freeholder has granted formal written consent. No change of use or structural alteration is proposed. The system is intended to enhance indoor comfort, air quality, and energy performance while preserving the building’s residential character.\n\nSupporting documentation includes:\n- Manufacturer datasheets (Midea AG Eco & Multi-Split)\n- Building regulation compliance evidence (Installation quote from qualified and insured contractor)\n- Noise/Vibration details - Manufacturer noise and vibration specifications\n- Annotated location and elevation diagrams\n- Freeholder consent\n- Site plans",
